From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:49:31 +0300
Subject: ES_LOW_MEMORY: cheap ship outlines by default (the full outline
 filter runs the nv40 fragment program out of temporaries)

On the PS3 (ps3.602) Mesa's nv30 compiler printed 'out of temps!!' 36 times at the first
outline draw (nvfx_fragprog.c: 48 temporaries on nv4x; outline.frag unrolls 2 x 9 x 8 lookups).
The flight showed only the player's ship and the messages, no HUD, starfield, planet or asteroids.
The GL2 plugin already has outlineLite (8 lookups) behind the 'Cheap ship outlines' preference,
which the game only takes by itself when the full shader does not compile; it is on by default now.

diff --git a/source/Preferences.cpp b/source/Preferences.cpp
--- a/source/Preferences.cpp
+++ b/source/Preferences.cpp
@@ -236,6 +236,10 @@ void Preferences::Load()
 #ifdef ES_LOW_MEMORY
 	// Keeps the land, planet, star, outfit and thumbnail sprites out of memory until they are needed.
 	settings["Defer loading images"] = true;
+	// The full ship outline filter (144 texture lookups) needs more fragment program temporaries than
+	// the nv40 has (Mesa's nv30 driver: "out of temps", 36 times, and the HUD, the starfield and the
+	// planets did not show in the PS3's flight); outlineLite takes 8 lookups.
+	settings["Cheap ship outlines"] = true;
 #endif
 
 	DataFile prefs(Files::Config() / "preferences.txt");
